# Escape claims over the hand-written fixture; check.py in this directory
# documents what is asserted. The mark budget is unlimited for the fixture and
# bootstrap and bounded for p5 and phaser, where each frame pop would otherwise
# cost a full mark. The fixture groups are concatenated in a fixed order so the
# source bytes and allocation identities match the expected/ snapshot. Only the
# fixture runs --strict (snapshot comparison plus a check that every confined
# site was reached), because only it calls every one of its confined sites.
#
# RUN: cat %S/fixture/contents/*.js %S/fixture/primitives/*.js %S/fixture/escapes/*.js > %t.js
# RUN: python3 %S/check.py --oracle ctcompile-test-type-oracle --claims ctcompile-test-escape-claims --script %{monorepo}/tools/check/escape-oracle.py --corpus %t.js --work %t --name fixture --strict
